@Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5205
# After Case 01, copy the "id" from the response and paste it here for Cases 29 and 39:
@registrationId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# Car Show Registration API - sample test scenarios (section 3G).
# Run them top to bottom, then tick Pass. Plate numbers must be unique, so on a re-run
# delete carshow.db (or change the TST plates).

# ===== 1. Make a new registration (POST /api/registrations) =====

### Case 01 - Valid Competitor, partly paid
# Expected: 201 Created, CS27-xxxx, fee 2500.00, Pending, Partial
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1001",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 02 - Valid Exhibitor, not paid
# Expected: 201 Created, fee 1500.00, Unpaid, Pending
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1002",
  "registrationType": "Exhibitor",
  "amountPaid": 0.00
}

### Case 03 - Valid VIP, fully paid
# Expected: 201 Created, fee 5000.00, Paid
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1003",
  "registrationType": "VIP",
  "amountPaid": 5000.00
}

### Case 04 - Registration numbers increase: compare the numbers returned by Case 01, 02 and 03 (consecutive).

### Case 05 - Client tries to set server-only fields (ignored)
# Expected: 201 Created, fee 5000.00, status Pending, next CS27-xxxx
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1005",
  "registrationType": "VIP",
  "amountPaid": 0.00,
  "registrationFee": 1,
  "status": "Confirmed",
  "registrationNumber": "HACK-1"
}

### Case 06 - All text fields empty
# Expected: 400 with errors for all six fields
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "",
  "contactNumber": "",
  "email": "",
  "address": "",
  "carMakeModel": "",
  "plateNumber": "",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 07 - Invalid contact number
# Expected: 400, errors.ContactNumber
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "12345",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1007",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 08 - Invalid email
# Expected: 400, errors.Email
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan-at-example",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1008",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 09 - Paid more than the fee
# Expected: 400, errors.AmountPaid (cannot be more than the fee 1,500)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1009",
  "registrationType": "Exhibitor",
  "amountPaid": 2000.00
}

### Case 10 - Negative amount paid
# Expected: 400, errors.AmountPaid (must be 0 or more)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1010",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": -100.00
}

### Case 11 - Unknown registration type
# Expected: 400, nothing created
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1011",
  "registrationType": "Sponsor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 12 - Participant name longer than 150 characters
# Expected: 400, errors.ParticipantName mentions 150
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1012",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 13 - Duplicate plate number (same as Case 01)
# Expected: 409 Conflict, title Registration.Conflict, detail names the plate
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1001",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

# ===== 2. Show all registrations (GET /api/registrations) =====

### Case 14 - Default list
# Expected: 200, page 1, pageSize 10, totalCount >= 25
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Accept: application/json

### Case 15 - Newest first (same request as Case 14, check order)
# Expected: 200, Case 01-05 registrations on top
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Accept: application/json

### Case 16 - Second page, custom size
# Expected: 200, page 2, 5 items
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?page=2&pageSize=5
Accept: application/json

### Case 17 - Page past the end
# Expected: 200, items [], totalCount unchanged
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?page=999
Accept: application/json

### Case 18 - Invalid page
# Expected: 400, errors.Page
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?page=0
Accept: application/json

### Case 19 - Page size too large
# Expected: 400, errors.PageSize (1-50)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?pageSize=100
Accept: application/json

# ===== 3. Find by type, status and participant name =====

### Case 20 - Find by type
# Expected: 200, every item VIP
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?type=VIP
Accept: application/json

### Case 21 - Find by status
# Expected: 200, every item Confirmed
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?status=Confirmed
Accept: application/json

### Case 22 - Find by participant name
# Expected: 200, names contain juan, Case 01 included
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?participantName=juan
Accept: application/json

### Case 23 - Name search ignores case
# Expected: 200, same as Case 22
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?participantName=JUAN
Accept: application/json

### Case 24 - Partial name match
# Expected: 200, includes Juan Dela Cruz
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?participantName=dela
Accept: application/json

### Case 25 - Combined filters
# Expected: 200, matches all three filters
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?type=Competitor&status=Pending&participantName=juan
Accept: application/json

### Case 26 - No matches
# Expected: 200, items [], totalCount 0, totalPages 0
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?participantName=zzzzzz
Accept: application/json

### Case 27 - Invalid type
# Expected: 400
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?type=Sponsor
Accept: application/json

### Case 28 - Invalid status
# Expected: 400
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?status=Done
Accept: application/json

# ===== 4. Find registration by ID (GET /api/registrations/{id}) =====

### Case 29 - Existing ID (set @registrationId from Case 01)
# Expected: 200, same data as Case 01
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/{{registrationId}}
Accept: application/json

### Case 30 - ID that does not exist
# Expected: 404, title Registration.NotFound
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Accept: application/json

### Case 31 - Not a valid GUID
# Expected: 404, no route matches (no 500)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/abc
Accept: application/json

# ===== 5. KPI summary (GET /api/registrations/summary) =====

### Case 32-36 - Summary returns all fields, counts add up, money adds up, cancelled excluded
# Expected: 200
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/summary
Accept: application/json

### Case 37 - Summary updates after a new registration (run summary, this, then summary again)
# Expected: 201; then summary: total +1, pending +1, totalFees +1500, totalPayments +500, uncollected +1000
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1037",
  "registrationType": "Exhibitor",
  "amountPaid": 500.00
}

### Case 38 - /summary is not treated as an id
# Expected: 200 summary (not 404/400)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/summary
Accept: application/json

# ===== 6. Database persistence =====
# Case 39: note totalCount, stop the API, start it again, repeat GET /api/registrations and Case 29.
# Case 40: open carshow.db in DB Browser for SQLite and check the unique indexes on Registrations (PlateNumber, RegistrationNumber).
